<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>IELTS Exam Mode: Children's Play</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@supabase/supabase-js@2"></script>
    <style>
        :root { --bg: #ffffff; --text: #1a1a1a; --sidebar: #f8f9fa; --accent: #2563eb; --highlight: #fff176; }
        body.dark-mode { --bg: #121212; --text: #e0e0e0; --sidebar: #1e1e1e; --accent: #4dabf7; }
        body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); margin: 0; display: flex; height: 100vh; overflow: hidden; transition: 0.3s; }
        
        .toolbar { position: fixed; top: 0; width: 100%; height: 60px; background: var(--sidebar); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 0 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; z-index: 100; box-sizing: border-box; }
        .container { display: flex; width: 100%; margin-top: 60px; height: calc(100vh - 60px); }
        .passage-area, .question-area { flex: 1; overflow-y: auto; padding: 40px; scroll-behavior: smooth; }
        .passage-area { border-right: 1px solid #ddd; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 18px; }
        
        .nav-grid { width: 70px; background: var(--sidebar); display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; padding-top: 20px; border-left: 1px solid #ddd; }
        .q-num { width: 35px; height: 35px; border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; margin-bottom: 12px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: bold; }
        .q-num.filled { background: var(--accent); color: white; }

        #hl-btn { position: absolute; display: none; background: #000; color: #fff; border: none; padding: 5px 10px; border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer; z-index: 500; }
        .highlighted { background: var(--highlight); color: #000; }

        .q-block { margin-bottom: 35px; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.02); }
        input[type="text"] { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 8px; border-radius: 4px; width: 200px; background: transparent; color: var(--text); }
        .feedback { display: none; margin-top: 10px; font-weight: bold; }
        .explanation { display: none; margin-top: 10px; font-style: italic; color: #555; font-size: 0.9em; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 10px; }

        .btn-submit { background: #16a34a; color: white; padding: 15px 40px; border: none; border-radius: 6px; cursor: pointer; font-size: 18px; margin: 40px 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="toolbar">
    <div>
        <button onclick="document.body.classList.toggle('dark-mode')">🌓 Toggle Theme</button>
        <button onclick="adjustFont(1)">A+</button>
        <button onclick="adjustFont(-1)">A-</button>
    </div>
    <div id="timer" style="font-weight: bold; font-size: 20px;">20:00</div>
    <button onclick="window.location.href='index.html'">Main Menu</button>
</div>

<button id="hl-btn">Highlight</button>

<div class="container">
    <div class="passage-area" id="passage-content">
        <h1>The Importance of Children’s Play</h1>
        <p id="p1">Brick by brick, six-year-old Alice is building a magical kingdom... creating an enchanting world. Although she isn’t aware of it, this fantasy is helping her take her first steps towards her capacity for <strong>creativity</strong> and so it will have important repercussions in her adult life.</p>
        <p id="p2">Minutes later, Alice has abandoned the kingdom in favour of playing schools... she’s learning about the need to follow <strong>rules</strong> and take turns with a partner.</p>
        <p id="p3">‘Play in all its rich variety is one of the highest achievements...’ says Dr David Whitebread... cruical to our success as a highly adaptable species.</p>
        <p id="p4">Recognizing the importance of play is not new... the Greek philosopher Plato extolled its virtues...</p>
        <p id="p5">...Whitebread is mindful of a worldwide decline in play, pointing out that over half the people in the world now live in <strong>cities</strong>. Outdoor play is curtailed by perceptions of risk to do with <strong>traffic</strong>, as well as parents’ increased wish to protect their children from <strong>crime</strong>, and by the emphasis on ‘earlier is better’ leading to greater <strong>competition</strong> in academic learning.</p>
        <p id="p6">...But what they often lack is the <strong>evidence</strong> to base policies on.</p>
        <p id="p7">...And we want to know what the long-term impact of play is. It’s a real challenge.</p>
        <p id="p8">...there is very little data on the impact it has on the child’s later <strong>life</strong>.</p>
        <p id="p9">...the ability to self-regulate has been shown to be a key predictor of academic performance.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="question-area">
        <h2>Questions 1-8 (One Word Only)</h2>
        <div class="q-block" data-q="1">1. building a ‘magical kingdom’ may help develop <input type="text" id="q1"> <div class="feedback" id="f1"></div><div class="explanation">Para 1: "...steps towards her capacity for creativity."</div></div>
        <div class="q-block" data-q="2">2. board games involve <input type="text" id="q2"> and turn-taking <div class="feedback" id="f2"></div><div class="explanation">Para 2: "...need to follow rules and take turns."</div></div>
        <div class="q-block" data-q="3">3. population of <input type="text" id="q3"> have grown <div class="feedback" id="f3"></div><div class="explanation">Para 5: "...over half the people in the world now live in cities."</div></div>
        <div class="q-block" data-q="4">4. fear of <input type="text" id="q4"> (4/5 either order) <div class="feedback" id="f4"></div><div class="explanation">Para 5: "...risk to do with traffic."</div></div>
        <div class="q-block" data-q="5">5. fear of <input type="text" id="q5"> (4/5 either order) <div class="feedback" id="f5"></div><div class="explanation">Para 5: "...protect their children from being the victims of crime."</div></div>
        <div class="q-block" data-q="6">6. increased <input type="text" id="q6"> in schools <div class="feedback" id="f6"></div><div class="explanation">Para 5: "...leading to greater competition in academic learning."</div></div>
        <div class="q-block" data-q="7">7. difficult to find <input type="text" id="q7"> to support policies <div class="feedback" id="f7"></div><div class="explanation">Para 6: "...what they often lack is the evidence."</div></div>
        <div class="q-block" data-q="8">8. impact of play on the rest of the child’s <input type="text" id="q8"> <div class="feedback" id="f8"></div><div class="explanation">Para 8: "...impact it has on the child’s later life."</div></div>

        <h2>Questions 9-13 (TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN)</h2>
        <div class="q-block" data-q="9">9. Self-control is a predictor of school success. <br><input type="checkbox" name="q9" value="TRUE"> T <input type="checkbox" name="q9" value="FALSE"> F <input type="checkbox" name="q9" value="NOT GIVEN"> NG <div class="feedback" id="f9"></div><div class="explanation">Para 13: Self-regulation is a key predictor of academic performance.</div></div>
        <div class="q-block" data-q="10">10. Play helps diagnose medical problems. <br><input type="checkbox" name="q10" value="TRUE"> T <input type="checkbox" name="q10" value="FALSE"> F <input type="checkbox" name="q10" value="NOT GIVEN"> NG <div class="feedback" id="f10"></div><div class="explanation">Para 14: Useful in the diagnosis of neurodevelopmental disorders.</div></div>
        <div class="q-block" data-q="11">11. Dolls benefit girls more than boys. <br><input type="checkbox" name="q11" value="TRUE"> T <input type="checkbox" name="q11" value="FALSE"> F <input type="checkbox" name="q11" value="NOT GIVEN"> NG <div class="feedback" id="f11"></div><div class="explanation">The passage does not compare genders for doll play.</div></div>
        <div class="q-block" data-q="12">12. Lego created problems for ideas. <br><input type="checkbox" name="q12" value="TRUE"> T <input type="checkbox" name="q12" value="FALSE"> F <input type="checkbox" name="q12" value="NOT GIVEN"> NG <div class="feedback" id="f12"></div><div class="explanation">Para 15: Not a single child said they didn't know what to write.</div></div>
        <div class="q-block" data-q="13">13. Play is seen as less significant today. <br><input type="checkbox" name="q13" value="TRUE"> T <input type="checkbox" name="q13" value="FALSE"> F <input type="checkbox" name="q13" value="NOT GIVEN"> NG <div class="feedback" id="f13"></div><div class="explanation">Para 17: "Somehow the importance of play has been lost in recent decades."</div></div>

        <button class="btn-submit" onclick="finishExam()">Finish Exam</button>
    </div>

    <div class="nav-grid" id="nav-grid"></div>
</div>

<script>
    const sb = supabase.createClient('https://evhceswvapszaghnvmxl.supabase.co', 'eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImV2aGNlc3d2YXBzemFnaG52bXhsIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3Nzc3OTQwNzMsImV4cCI6MjA5MzM3MDA3M30.yV7tavgR7JKc45uSGtS8Lf6m1ZMuuvQ23hmAb8n6k3A');
    
    const keys = {
        q1: btoa('creativity'), q2: btoa('rules'), q3: btoa('cities'), q4: btoa('traffic|crime'), q5: btoa('traffic|crime'), 
        q6: btoa('competition'), q7: btoa('evidence'), q8: btoa('life'), q9: btoa('TRUE'), q10: btoa('TRUE'), 
        q11: btoa('NOT GIVEN'), q12: btoa('FALSE'), q13: btoa('TRUE')
    };

    // UI Logic
    let fSize = 18;
    function adjustFont(v) { fSize = Math.min(24, Math.max(14, fSize + v)); document.getElementById('passage-content').style.fontSize = fSize + 'px'; }

    // Highlight Logic
    const hlBtn = document.getElementById('hl-btn');
    document.addEventListener('mouseup', e => {
        const sel = window.getSelection();
        if (sel.toString().length > 0) { hlBtn.style.display='block'; hlBtn.style.left=e.pageX+'px'; hlBtn.style.top=e.pageY+'px'; }
        else hlBtn.style.display='none';
    });
    hlBtn.onclick = () => {
        const range = window.getSelection().getRangeAt(0);
        const span = document.createElement('span'); span.className='highlighted';
        range.surroundContents(span); hlBtn.style.display='none';
    };

    // Sidebar Init
    const grid = document.getElementById('nav-grid');
    for(let i=1; i<=13; i++) {
        const d = document.createElement('div'); d.className='q-num'; d.innerText=i; d.id='nav'+i;
        grid.appendChild(d);
    }

    // Mutex Checkboxes
    document.querySelectorAll('input[type="checkbox"]').forEach(cb => {
        cb.onchange = () => {
            document.getElementsByName(cb.name).forEach(o => { if(o!==cb) o.checked=false; });
            document.getElementById('nav'+cb.name.substring(1)).classList.add('filled');
        };
    });
    document.querySelectorAll('input[type="text"]').forEach(ti => {
        ti.oninput = () => { if(ti.value.length > 0) document.getElementById('nav'+ti.id.substring(1)).classList.add('filled'); };
    });

    // Submit Logic
    async function finishExam() {
        let score = 0;
        for(let i=1; i<=13; i++) {
            let val = "";
            const textInput = document.getElementById('q'+i);
            if(textInput) val = textInput.value.trim().toLowerCase();
            else {
                const checked = document.querySelector(`input[name="q${i}"]:checked`);
                if(checked) val = checked.value;
            }

            const correct = atob(keys['q'+i]).toLowerCase().split('|');
            if(correct.includes(val)) {
                score++;
                document.getElementById('f'+i).innerText = "✅ Correct";
                document.getElementById('f'+i).style.color = "green";
            } else {
                document.getElementById('f'+i).innerText = "❌ Incorrect";
                document.getElementById('f'+i).style.color = "red";
                document.querySelectorAll('.explanation')[i-1].style.display = "block";
            }
            document.getElementById('f'+i).style.display = "block";
        }

        const band = ((score/13)*9).toFixed(1);
        const { data: { user } } = await sb.auth.getUser();
        if(user) {
            await sb.from('scores').upsert({ user_id: user.id, passage_id: 'the-importance-of-childrens-play', score: band });
        }
        alert("Your Score: " + band);
        document.querySelectorAll('input').forEach(i => i.disabled = true);
    }

    // Timer
    let t = 1200;
    setInterval(() => { if(t>0) { t--; let m=Math.floor(t/60), s=t%60; document.getElementById('timer').innerText=`${m}:${s<10?'0'+s:s}`; } }, 1000);
</script>

</body>
</html>
